<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tazeroualt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tazeroualt is a region in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anti-atlas">Anti-Atlas</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sous">Sous</a> valley. It holds the shrine of the 16th-century saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidi-ahmed-ou-moussa">Sidi Ahmed ou Moussa</a>, and in the 17th century his descendants made Iligh the capital of a sharifate that controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a> and the Atlantic coast. The family remained influential local lords into the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tazeroualt.jpg" alt="Tazeroualt" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucyin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zawiya_Sidi_Ahmed_ou_Moussa_tombe-tchapele_payizaedje_Tazerwalt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
